; bfsodium ChaCha20 STREAM CIPHER  RFC 8439 section 2 point 4
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The block function  the exclusive or and the adder that
; steps the block counter are each PASTED ONCE from their own verified files
; rather than written out again  so this file is the plumbing and nothing else;
;
; IO  in:  key{32}  counter{4} LE  nonce{12}  len{2} LE  plaintext{len}
;     out: ciphertext{len}
;
; The length prefix is how the program knows when to stop; a bfsodium primitive
; never relies on end of input;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x10f  the block routine's whole frame; its footprint is 0:271 and
;                 tools/bffoot proves that against its instruction stream; the
;                 forty eight bytes it works from go in at @0x010:0x03f and the
;                 keystream comes back at @0x000:0x03f
;   @0x060:0x08f  copy temps; these live INSIDE that frame and are emptied
;                 before it is entered  which the contract below states
;   @0x120:0x14f  saved{48}  key{32} @0x120  counter{4} @0x140  nonce{12} @0x144
;   @0x150:0x151  remaining{2} u16 LE  message bytes still to emit
;   @0x152        nz     set while remaining is not zero
;   @0x153        j      keystream bytes left in this block
;   @0x154        e      the else arm of the borrowing decrement
;   @0x155        t      a copy  so a count can be tested without being eaten
;   @0x156        u      puts that copy back
;   @0x157        f      set while the keystream is spent
;   @0x160:0x179  the exclusive or frame; xor32 footprint 0:25 at @0x160
;   @0x180:0x18d  the adder frame; add32 footprint 0:13 at @0x180
;
; One turn of the loop is ONE message byte; a block is made only when the last
; one has been used up  so the tail of a message needs no special case and no
; division: the count simply runs out partway through a block;
;
; The exclusive or is xor32 rather than a byte sized one  with the upper three
; bytes of both operands left at zero; It costs four times the bit work for one
; byte  which against ten double rounds of ChaCha per sixty four bytes is not
; measurable  and it means no new bitwise routine had to be written and proved;

; ==== read the key  counter  nonce and the length ====
>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; continued
  >,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; continued
  >,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; the two byte length prefix
>
  ,>,
